["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"entity-runtime","stream_identity":"01a0d359-c9cc-77a1-9251-a0c4fa10446c","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"architecture-decision-record","fields":{"body":"# ADR: The repository is called entity-runtime\n\n## Status\n\nProposed 2026-08-25. The name was chosen by the agent under the operator's instruction to decide\nand report; a rename before the first push costs a directory move and one line in `atlas`.\n\n## Context\n\n`atlas/AGENTS.md`: repos are plain lowercase nouns naming their function. The naming conversation\nthat produced the proof of concept ended on *Entity Runtime* for a system whose objects have\nschemas, lifecycles, operations, invariants and events.\n\n## Decision\n\n`entity-runtime`. It names the function (a runtime for entities), it is the term the proof of\nconcept settled on, and it does not collide with a type or crate in `engineering-protocols`, where\n*entity* is the universal model this kernel would execute.\n\n## Alternatives\n\n* **`object-platform` / `object-runtime`** — the broadest names from the conversation; rejected as\n  naming the ambition rather than the thing built.\n* **`entity-engine`, `aggregate-runtime`, `domain-runtime`** — accurate; rejected for jargon\n  (`aggregate`) or vagueness (`domain`).\n* **`decider`** — the functional name for decide/evolve; rejected as obscure.\n* **`lifecycle`** — a single noun naming the defining feature; rejected because the runtime is also\n  the schema, the rules and the events, and because `artifacts/lifecycles/` exists in\n  `engineering-protocols` with a narrower meaning.\n\n## Consequences\n\nCrate names follow: `entity-core`, `entity-yaml`, `entity-cli`; the binary is `entity`. The\n`atlas` map carries the row.\n","document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"ent-bf6470783cc7d0fd34a74bfc6e5ba91e","locator":"ep://planning/store/architecture-decision-record/repository-name","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":2,"type":"aep.architecture-decision-record/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"# ADR: The repository is called entity-runtime\n\n## Status\n\nProposed 2026-08-25. The name was chosen by the agent under the operator's instruction to decide\nand report; a rename before the first push costs a directory move and one line in `atlas`.\n\n## Context\n\n`atlas/AGENTS.md`: repos are plain lowercase nouns naming their function. The naming conversation\nthat produced the proof of concept ended on *Entity Runtime* for a system whose objects have\nschemas, lifecycles, operations, invariants and events.\n\n## Decision\n\n`entity-runtime`. It names the function (a runtime for entities), it is the term the proof of\nconcept settled on, and it does not collide with a type or crate in `engineering-protocols`, where\n*entity* is the universal model this kernel would execute.\n\n## Alternatives\n\n* **`object-platform` / `object-runtime`** — the broadest names from the conversation; rejected as\n  naming the ambition rather than the thing built.\n* **`entity-engine`, `aggregate-runtime`, `domain-runtime`** — accurate; rejected for jargon\n  (`aggregate`) or vagueness (`domain`).\n* **`decider`** — the functional name for decide/evolve; rejected as obscure.\n* **`lifecycle`** — a single noun naming the defining feature; rejected because the runtime is also\n  the schema, the rules and the events, and because `artifacts/lifecycles/` exists in\n  `engineering-protocols` with a narrower meaning.\n\n## Consequences\n\nCrate names follow: `entity-core`, `entity-yaml`, `entity-cli`; the binary is `entity`. The\n`atlas` map carries the row.\n","relations":[{"decides":"epic:kernel"}],"status":"proposed","summary":"Chosen over object platform, entity engine, aggregate runtime, domain runtime, decider and lifecycle.","title":"The repository is called entity-runtime"},"lifecycle_state":"proposed"},"relations":[{"decides":"epic:kernel"}],"summary":"Chosen over object platform, entity engine, aggregate runtime, domain runtime, decider and lifecycle.","title":"The repository is called entity-runtime"},"id":"ent-bf6470783cc7d0fd34a74bfc6e5ba91e","lifecycle_state":"proposed","revision":2,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["architecture-decision-record","ent-bf6470783cc7d0fd34a74bfc6e5ba91e"]}]